KNOWNBUG gcc-only
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ typeof subscript: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
GCC's typeof extension: `__typeof__(a[0])' names the type of the expression
a[0].  The front end reports "found no match for symbol 'a'";
`__typeof__(a)' and `decltype(a[0])' work.  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
